chapter AFP

(* The Isabelle/occam manual, a sub-session of "Occam2" (../ROOT): it imports
   the global theory "Occam2" and runs its live examples against the real
   commands. Being a session of its own, it also needs no import edge to the
   test theories to be kept apart from them (the lexer state is process-wide,
   see the Limitations section of the manual).

   Generate the PDF with

     isabelle build -d occam2 Occam2_Manual

   which writes "manual/output/document.pdf" ("output" is git-ignored). The
   LaTeX sources are in "document/": "root.tex" (the same style as the C11
   manual, uses the lualatex/fontspec setup of Isabelle's own document build)
   and "root.bib" (copied from the C11 project, plus the occam 2 reference
   manual). *)
session "Occam2_Manual" (AFP) = "Occam2" +
  options [timeout = 1200, document = pdf, document_output = "output"]
  theories
    Occam2_Manual
  document_files
    "root.tex"
    "root.bib"
